|---|---|---|
| Magnitude of winter NHS problem | 4 | Mental health presentations contribute significantly to A&E crowding, particularly over festive periods; CAMHS winter pressures also significant |
| Strength of evidence | 3 | Psychiatric liaison evidence positive for LOS reduction (Parsonage et al., 2012); 24/7 crisis lines evidence moderate; CRHTTs evidence mixed on diverting admissions |
| Cost-effectiveness | 3 | Liaison psychiatry clearly cost-effective in general hospital settings (RAID model; Parsonage & Fossey, 2011); community crisis care ROI less established |
| NHS/Life Sciences alignment | 4 | NHS Mental Health Five Year Forward View; NHS LTP MH commitments; NHS Crisis Care Concordat |
| Temporal impact | 3 | Short-term: liaison reduces LOS; Medium-term: system requires significant workforce investment |
| Health inequalities impact | 5 | Mental health burden disproportionate in deprived communities; BAME communities under-served; crisis care inequalities substantial |

