#### RANK 2: Respiratory Disease Early Detection, Prevention and Management
**Score: 90/100 | Confidence: High**

**Why it qualifies:**
- **Magnitude:** COPD and pneumonia are consistently in the top 5 causes of emergency admissions nationally; lower respiratory tract infections are the leading cause of infection-related mortality in winter
- **Evidence strength:** NICE guidelines NG115 (COPD) and NG191 (Asthma) provide strong evidence-based pathways; pulmonary rehabilitation has Cochrane support (McCarthy et al., 2015); targeted COPD case-finding supported by growing UK evidence (Roberts et al., 2021)
- **Cost-effectiveness:** Pulmonary rehabilitation is one of the most cost-effective NHS interventions for COPD; each avoided exacerbation saves approximately £1,700 in emergency care (BTS/BLF data)
- **NHS/Life Sciences alignment:** NHS RightCare respiratory pathway; NHS LTP cancer/respiratory diagnostic programme; NHS Accelerated Access Collaborative inhaler optimisation work
- **Temporal impact:** Short-term: exacerbation management; Medium-term: PR capacity building; Long-term: population case-finding impact
- **Health inequalities:** Respiratory disease burden is steeply socially graded; smoking cessation, cold homes, and occupational exposures are inequality drivers — interventions in this space directly address health inequalities

